From b6a65b95e04ed03b869ff56cf1845038bb74a82f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:04:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: i2s-tdm: Register the PCM before the DAI

A card that was registered before its CPU DAI is put on the unbind list
by snd_soc_bind_card(), and snd_soc_add_component() retries the bind as
soon as any component is added. The DAI component of the I2S controller
satisfies the DAI link's platform, which defaults to the CPU of_node, so
the card binds right after the DAI is registered and before the dmaengine
PCM component of the same device exists. The PCM component is then never
added to the runtime, runtime->hw stays empty and every open of the PCM
fails with -EINVAL from snd_pcm_hw_constraints_complete(), without any
error being logged.

This is seen on RK3588 when the HDMI codec probes before the I2S
controller of the HDMI sound card: the card has no "dma:fddf0000.i2s"
component and "aplay -D hw:0,0" fails with "Invalid argument".

Register the dmaengine PCM first, as rockchip_spdif already does, so the
card finds both components when the DAI appears.

Fixes: 081068fd6414 ("ASoC: rockchip: add support for i2s-tdm controller")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c
index 610bf65d017a..2178fcdc0530 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s_tdm.c
@@ -1359,13 +1359,18 @@ static int rockchip_i2s_tdm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (i2s_tdm->soc_data && i2s_tdm->soc_data->init)
 		i2s_tdm->soc_data->init(&pdev->dev, res->start);
 
-	ret = devm_snd_soc_register_component(&pdev->dev,
-					      &rockchip_i2s_tdm_component,
-					      i2s_tdm->dai, 1);
+	/*
+	 * Register the PCM before the DAI: adding the DAI component can bind a
+	 * waiting card right away, and the card must find the PCM component
+	 * then or its DAI link ends up without one.
+	 */
+	ret = devm_snd_dmaengine_pcm_register(&pdev->dev, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_suspend;
 
-	ret = devm_snd_dmaengine_pcm_register(&pdev->dev, NULL, 0);
+	ret = devm_snd_soc_register_component(&pdev->dev,
+					      &rockchip_i2s_tdm_component,
+					      i2s_tdm->dai, 1);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_suspend;
 
